-- expected_rows --
[]
-- description --
histogram_quantile over min_over_time of a classic bucket selector, with no aggregation, one quantile per series.
Prometheus reads each `le` rung of a classic histogram as an ordinary float
series, so min_over_time reduces every rung to the smallest cumulative count in the window
before the quantile interpolates the ladder. The three samples of each series
carry different ladders, so each over-time function lands on a different
quantile. The matcher once accepted only rate, increase and sum_over_time, and
this shape fell through to the non-bucket fallback, which answers an empty
vector.
